{"name":"Fire Axe Red","hex":"#ce1620","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (usually self-sustaining) chemical reaction involving the bonding of oxygen with carbon or other fuel, with the production of heat and the presence of flame or smouldering.","An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and maintained in a specific location to a useful end (such as a campfire or a hearth fire)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Amazing; excellent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire"},{"term":"axe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ayerrerenge."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tool for felling trees or chopping wood etc. consisting of a heavy  head flattened to a blade on one side, and a  handle attached to it.","An ancient weapon consisting of a  head that has one or two blades and a long handle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/axe"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Axe","blocks":[{"text":"An axe is an implement that has been used for thousands of years to shape, split, and cut wood, to harvest timber, and as a weapon. The axe has many forms and specialised uses but generally consists of a head with a sharpened blade attached to a handle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Felling_axe.jpg/330px-Felling_axe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axe"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg/500px-Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg/1280px-Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg/500px-Kokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bronze socketed axe from the Heppeneert hoard (Belgium), about 800 BCE, collection of the King Baudouin Foundation, Gallo-Roman Museum (Tongeren)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKokerbijl_van_het_Plainseautype_in_brons%2C_925_tot_800_VC%2C_vindplaats-_Maaseik%2C_Heppeneert%2C_Wayerveld%2C_collectie_Gallo-Romeins_Museum_Tongeren%2C_He_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/ALB_-_Hortfund_Gro%C3%9F_Gaglow.jpg/500px-ALB_-_Hortfund_Gro%C3%9F_Gaglow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/ALB_-_Hortfund_Gro%C3%9F_Gaglow.jpg/1280px-ALB_-_Hortfund_Gro%C3%9F_Gaglow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/ALB_-_Hortfund_Gro%C3%9F_Gaglow.j